    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the subscript $o$ denotes the observed scale, and $\\sigma^{2}(A_{o})$ is the additive genetic variance on the observed scale. In an appendix to Dempster and Lerner (1950), Robertson showed that $\\sigma^{2}(A_{o}) \\simeq [p(x_{p})]^{2}h^{2}$, where $h^{2}$ is the heritability on the unobserved scale of liability. Thus, the relationship between the heritabilities on the underlying and observed scales is",
      "source_page": 754,
      "printed_page": 734,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter25:p016:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        138.0,
